 1: {"ind": 27212, "activity_label": "Discus throw", "ctx_a": "A man with a blue shirt, blue sweat pants and green socks is standing outside in a large field walking into a circle of cement. Once the guy is on the circle, he begins walking around the circle to find his perfect spot.", "ctx_b": "everything", "ctx": "A man with a blue shirt, blue sweat pants and green socks is standing outside in a large field walking into a circle of cement. Once the guy is on the circle, he begins walking around the circle to find his perfect spot. everything", "split": "val", "split_type": "indomain", "label": 3, "endings": ["starts to look very interesting as he begins to bump into the wall and fall into it.", "is as she was gone, she was standing then spinning around a few times.", "is in place as he grabs the end of the hopscotch stick with his foot and uses it to move towards the outline of the jump.", "is perfect and then he throws the discus that was in his hand into the field as he is spinning around."], "source_id": "activitynet~v_mpC_UTM1tWQ"}
 2: {"ind": 41678, "ctx": "[header] How to avoid using personal language in writing [title] Use the third person point of view. [step] Never use \" i, \" \" my, \" or otherwise refer to yourself in formal academic writing. You should also avoid using the second person point of view, such as by referring to the reader as \" you.", "activity_label": "Education and Communications", "ctx_a": "[header] How to avoid using personal language in writing [title] Use the third person point of view. [step] Never use \" i, \" \" my, \" or otherwise refer to yourself in formal academic writing. You should also avoid using the second person point of view, such as by referring to the reader as \" you.", "ctx_b": "", "split": "val", "split_type": "indomain", "label": 3, "endings": ["\" [substeps] If you are asked a question, try to find something that can be answered by simply ending the discussion with an \" i \" instead of the second person point of view. For example, if a reader asked if you were ethically related, you can answer that question.", "\" in a lot of academic writing, you will add to the title of the essay using third person to show that you are the reader instead of the author. Using this method helps make in-text manuscripts cool and collected, rather than essay paper expressing your thesis, so you can apply this to the entire essay.", "\" [substeps] Always use the third person point of view while using \" i. \" this is the third person point of view used in formal writing, not \" you.", "\" instead, write directly about your subject matter in the third person. [substeps] For example, replace \" i think the most important part of your day is having a good breakfast, \" with \" a nutritious breakfast is an important part of a healthy diet."], "source_id": "wikihow~68605"}
 3: {"ind": 29700, "ctx": "[header] How to pamper yourself at home [title] Run yourself a hot bath. [step] Check the temperature to make sure that it isn't too hot. Add some rose or lavender oil to the bath to soothe your mind and relax.", "activity_label": "Personal Care and Style", "ctx_a": "[header] How to pamper yourself at home [title] Run yourself a hot bath. [step] Check the temperature to make sure that it isn't too hot. Add some rose or lavender oil to the bath to soothe your mind and relax.", "ctx_b": "", "split": "val", "split_type": "zeroshot", "label": 3, "endings": ["Lather your hair with the warm water. Start by tensing your muscles, holding a deep breath.", "Then, put your soaking clothes and relaxing medicine into the warm bath. Heat the water to the right temperature before you put your hand in and take a few deep breaths.", "Turn on some music and soak in it for a few minutes. [title] Draw or edit pictures of yourself online.", "You could also use some lavender scented bubble bath. Dim the lights in your bathroom so it's darker or just go by candlelight."], "source_id": "wikihow~48971"}
 4: {"ind": 20776, "activity_label": "Running a marathon", "ctx_a": "People run in a marathon in the street. A man head the race and run alone in the street.", "ctx_b": "suddenly", "ctx": "People run in a marathon in the street. A man head the race and run alone in the street. suddenly", "split": "val", "split_type": "zeroshot", "label": 1, "endings": [", a dog with missing front paws walks chasing after the man.", ", the man crashes into the car and falls.", ", it ends running in different directions.", ", two runners run in the same race."], "source_id": "activitynet~v_6okx-34bDEg"}
 5: {"ind": 5408, "ctx": "[header] How to remedy hemorrhoids with simple folk medicine [title] Purchase witch hazel. [step] You can find it at the store in the liquid astringent form (typically in 12 ounce bottles) and a tub of baby wipes, but do not toss it in a toilet. It's best to use wipes that are toilet safe by charmin or other companies.", "activity_label": "Health", "ctx_a": "[header] How to remedy hemorrhoids with simple folk medicine [title] Purchase witch hazel. [step] You can find it at the store in the liquid astringent form (typically in 12 ounce bottles) and a tub of baby wipes, but do not toss it in a toilet. It's best to use wipes that are toilet safe by charmin or other companies.", "ctx_b": "", "split": "val", "split_type": "indomain", "label": 1, "endings": ["[substeps] Witch hazel alone does not correct hemorrhoids, so read the packaging carefully. If you don't like the way it smells, put some witch hazel into your toilet twice a day.", "Some refills also contain a new tub. [title] Add the witch hazel to the wipes.", "[substeps] Wash your hands first with hand sanitizer before using witch hazel, and squeeze the alcohol back into the bottle. Add \u00bd tablespoon (30 ml) of witch hazel to half of a glass of milk.", "[title] Wash your hands with warm water and soap. [step] Pour witch hazel from the distilled container over your hands and then run the water over your hands, scrubbing your hands."], "source_id": "wikihow~8988"}
 6: {"ind": 6327, "ctx": "[header] How to clean stainmaster carpet [title] Vacuum the dirt. [step] First, you can remove a lot of the dirt with a vacuum cleaner. Then, you can tackle the remaining stains with soap and water.", "activity_label": "Home and Garden", "ctx_a": "[header] How to clean stainmaster carpet [title] Vacuum the dirt. [step] First, you can remove a lot of the dirt with a vacuum cleaner. Then, you can tackle the remaining stains with soap and water.", "ctx_b": "", "split": "val", "split_type": "indomain", "label": 2, "endings": ["Then, start dusting and vacuuming. Don't use any harsh chemicals, like abrasive scrubbing or cleaners, as these can actually cause mold to grow on the carpet.", "[substeps] Have your duster surface dusted before you vacuum. You may do this with a microfiber cloth or a brush.", "[title] Use soap and water on the stain. [step] Mix water and \u00bc cup (21 grams) of liquid soap into a spray bottle, and then spray this mixture directly onto the stain.", "Look for mud or black marks that you can spot clean. [substeps] If your stainmaster carpet isn't spotless, then it may need to be cleaned by a professional."], "source_id": "wikihow~10444"}
 7: {"ind": 46019, "ctx": "[header] How to watch a movie [title] Play dvds through your player or computer to watch movies simply and easily. [step] If you have a physical copy of the movie, simply put it in to play it. You will need to appropriate device, of course.", "activity_label": "Holidays and Traditions", "ctx_a": "[header] How to watch a movie [title] Play dvds through your player or computer to watch movies simply and easily. [step] If you have a physical copy of the movie, simply put it in to play it. You will need to appropriate device, of course.", "ctx_b": "", "split": "val", "split_type": "indomain", "label": 0, "endings": ["Almost all computers and laptops can handle dvds now, and many can handle blu-ray without a hiccup. Most video game systems, too, can play blu-ray/dvd.", "You can select not to screen movie files or to play the movies yourself. [title] Put in headphones, video games and even tea bags and coffee filters to get in order to watch the movie at night.", "[title] Never keep kids quiet on a video. [step] Video games read full movies, not drags all night.", "[title] Find a place where you can watch your files and docusate it online. [step] Place the location in your player's sd card as well to minimize that screen time."], "source_id": "wikihow~75767"}
 8: {"ind": 12182, "ctx": "[header] How to make a cheerleading ponytail [title] Make sure your hair is clean, but not wet. [step] Creating hairstyles on wet hair can cause breakage, especially on thick hair. It's a good idea to include conditioner as well as shampoo when washing your hair.", "activity_label": "Personal Care and Style", "ctx_a": "[header] How to make a cheerleading ponytail [title] Make sure your hair is clean, but not wet. [step] Creating hairstyles on wet hair can cause breakage, especially on thick hair. It's a good idea to include conditioner as well as shampoo when washing your hair.", "ctx_b": "", "split": "val", "split_type": "zeroshot", "label": 3, "endings": ["This is important for layering, so your hair will stay tight and would look silky under the hair stream. [substeps] You could use a clarifying shampoo to lift any tangles or frizz.", "[title] Place a shower cap over your hair after washing it. [step] Being in the shower may strip your hair of some moisture, and not only will this make your hair frizzier, but it can give you a chance to straighten.", "When your hair is wet, it's easier to keep a sleek, bouncy ponytail while you work to prevent breakage. [substeps] If your hair is damp from the shower, your hair will be wet, which increases frizz.", "[substeps] It is a good idea to create your ponytail on hair that is a day or two old of a wash, if manageable. [title] Put a hair elastic or two on your wrist."], "source_id": "wikihow~20102"}
 9: {"ind": 35749, "activity_label": "Brushing teeth", "ctx_a": "A small boy brushes his teeth at a bathroom sink. The boy stops brushing his teeth and starts manipulating the buttons on the electric toothbrush.", "ctx_b": "the boy", "ctx": "A small boy brushes his teeth at a bathroom sink. The boy stops brushing his teeth and starts manipulating the buttons on the electric toothbrush. the boy", "split": "val", "split_type": "indomain", "label": 0, "endings": ["rinses the toothbrush and his mouth with running tap water.", "returns to brushing the buttons and stops to glower at the camera.", "then picks up the razor and blows toothpaste down his chin.", "then stops brushing and turns the savetop back off."], "source_id": "activitynet~v_5OWJ7WqKWMU"}
10: {"ind": 10637, "activity_label": "Mooping floor", "ctx_a": "The man puts the mop into the blue mop bucket first and then he starts mopping.", "ctx_b": "first he", "ctx": "The man puts the mop into the blue mop bucket first and then he starts mopping. first he", "split": "val", "split_type": "indomain", "label": 2, "endings": ["sits down and scrubs his right leg with the mop again.", "continues mopping mopping tapping the wooden floor.", "mops near the stove and the counter.", "uses the mop to push all the hair away from his face."], "source_id": "activitynet~v_6QImnhUemH0"}
11: {"ind": 27697, "ctx": "[header] How to avoid scams abroad by learning a foreign language [title] Buy, rent, or borrow a set of language lessons. [step] You can get them on tape or cd, whichever medium you prefer. [title] Listen to them.", "activity_label": "Education and Communications", "ctx_a": "[header] How to avoid scams abroad by learning a foreign language [title] Buy, rent, or borrow a set of language lessons. [step] You can get them on tape or cd, whichever medium you prefer. [title] Listen to them.", "ctx_b": "", "split": "val", "split_type": "indomain", "label": 3, "endings": ["[step] Teach them all the basics of the language except for those that you fear may be scams, like english. [title] Keep up to date on the real language.", "[step] Speak korean, french, german, italian, etc. [title] Take flash cards (such as a black, white or japanese set) and write out your language speaking answers (27 out of 31 questions in a set of 15 answering rounds).", "[step] Perhaps they will have better experience adapting to speaking the language. [title] If they say no, know that you have an interpreter.", "[step] Start at least a couple of weeks before your trip so you have time to make it through a course before you leave. [title] Check the state department's web site."], "source_id": "wikihow~45641"}
12: {"ind": 19794, "ctx": "[header] How to clean a fish bowl [title] Figure out how much water your bowl holds. [step] In order to determine how much clean water you'll need to prepare, you first need to gently pour the bowl's current water and the fish into a clean, soap-free bucket or container. Then, mark the water level on the outside of the bucket.", "activity_label": "Pets and Animals", "ctx_a": "[header] How to clean a fish bowl [title] Figure out how much water your bowl holds. [step] In order to determine how much clean water you'll need to prepare, you first need to gently pour the bowl's current water and the fish into a clean, soap-free bucket or container. Then, mark the water level on the outside of the bucket.", "ctx_b": "", "split": "val", "split_type": "indomain", "label": 2, "endings": ["This will give you specific guidelines about how much water each container should hold. Fill a bucket or container with warm, soapy water and set it underneath your bowl.", "[substeps] Only use water that is sterilized. The amount of clean water your bucket holds will vary with the amount of fish you intend to clean.", "[title] Figure out how much new water you'll need. [step] When you clean your fish bowl, you'll need to replace 40-50% of the total volume of water that it holds.", "Repeat this process for each gallon or liter of water that you use. [substeps] Be sure to record this number for easy reference."], "source_id": "wikihow~32683"}
13: {"ind": 11853, "ctx": "[header] How to load a frightened horse into a horse trailer [title] Prepare to load two horses together. [step] If your horse is of the trusting nature, having a friend might help him or her load. If you don't have a trailer that accommodates two or more horses, ask around your barn to see if you can borrow someone's for a few hours.", "activity_label": "Pets and Animals", "ctx_a": "[header] How to load a frightened horse into a horse trailer [title] Prepare to load two horses together. [step] If your horse is of the trusting nature, having a friend might help him or her load. If you don't have a trailer that accommodates two or more horses, ask around your barn to see if you can borrow someone's for a few hours.", "ctx_b": "", "split": "val", "split_type": "indomain", "label": 2, "endings": ["[substeps] You should give the friend or family member a call to let them know that you will be loading two horses together. This way, they can check in to make sure they trust you.", "[title] Get a bag large enough to hold your horse. [step] You'll be handling your frightened horse before he or she gets on and begins to run inside its trailer.", "[title] Load the other horse into the trailer first, making sure to tie him or her before leaving. [step] It's best to use a horse that loads well into trailers, so your horse will see that his/her friend isn't frightened.", "Asking around is an easy option, especially if the first friend you call might be too reckless. [substeps] Explain your situation to your trusted friend or family member when your horse is unloaded."], "source_id": "wikihow~19558"}

