     13: {"ind": 11853, "ctx": "[header] How to load a frightened horse into a horse trailer [title] Prepare to load two horses together. [step] If your horse is of the trusting nature, having a friend might help him or her load. If you don't have a trailer that accommodates two or more horses, ask around your barn to see if you can borrow someone's for a few hours.", "activity_label": "Pets and Animals", "ctx_a": "[header] How to load a frightened horse into a horse trailer [title] Prepare to load two horses together. [step] If your horse is of the trusting nature, having a friend might help him or her load. If you don't have a trailer that accommodates two or more horses, ask around your barn to see if you can borrow someone's for a few hours.", "ctx_b": "", "split": "val", "split_type": "indomain", "label": 2, "endings": ["[substeps] You should give the friend or family member a call to let them know that you will be loading two horses together. This way, they can check in to make sure they trust you.", "[title] Get a bag large enough to hold your horse. [step] You'll be handling your frightened horse before he or she gets on and begins to run inside its trailer.", "[title] Load the other horse into the trailer first, making sure to tie him or her before leaving. [step] It's best to use a horse that loads well into trailers, so your horse will see that his/her friend isn't frightened.", "Asking around is an easy option, especially if the first friend you call might be too reckless. [substeps] Explain your situation to your trusted friend or family member when your horse is unloaded."], "source_id": "wikihow~19558"}
